# Ad-hoc live-instance probe scripts. One-off tools written to poke a running
# instance during a debugging round; whatever they established belongs in a test,
# not in history. Committed tooling lives under scripts/ with a real name.
scripts/r[0-9]-*
scripts/r[0-9][0-9]-*
scripts/round2-*
scripts/staging*.py
scripts/debug-*
scripts/bind-test*.py
scripts/check-*.py
scripts/regression*.py
scripts/verify-binding.py
scripts/verify-cert.sh
scripts/test-route.py
scripts/diag.py
scripts/state.py

# Development data.
# Leading slashes matter here: without one, "acme/" matches a directory of that
# name at any depth, which silently swallowed three source files under
# internal/acme/ and left CI unable to build from a clean checkout. These entries
# are meant for the runtime data directories at the repo root only — /acme holds
# the ACME account key and must stay ignored.
.aegis/
.aegis-test/
/acme/
/data/

